/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  curate21_vp_diEthylCarbonate -- the vapour pressure of diEthylCarbonate, REFITTED to
  measurements (DEV.md 4c C281 and C283).  Written by `bin/choupo-curate vp
  diEthylCarbonate`; everything above the RESULT paragraph is the DECLARATION,
  committed before any fit ran, so it can be read against the result.

  WHY.  The catalogue record carried `vaporPressure { model AmbroseWalton; }`,
  a corresponding-states ESTIMATE from Tc, Pc and omega that never reads the
  record's own Tb (C279 measured a median 19.6 % AAD over the 25 such records
  with archive data).  Here a three-parameter Antoine is fitted to EVERY
  usable laboratory's measurements of it.

  STUDIES (one per article, extracted by `choupo-thermoml extract-vp`; ranked
  by points, ties by DOI):
      10.1016/j.jct.2008.02.012        44 pts  273.1-315.2 K  Kozlova; Emel'yanenko; Georgieva; Verevkin et al.
      10.1021/acs.jced.7b00295         42 pts  238.15-296.15 K  Pokorny; Stejfa; Fulem; Cervinka et al.
      10.1021/je200784y                33 pts  354.68-399.27 K  Marrufo; Loras; Lladosa
      10.1021/je800984q                21 pts  343.77-398.28 K  Xing; Fang; Li; Guo et al.
      10.1016/j.jct.2014.07.004        17 pts  277.96-353.15 K  Dougassa; Jacquemin; Ouatani; Tessier et al.
      10.1021/acs.jced.7b00236         10 pts  303.15-323.15 K  Anugraha; Altway; Wibawa
  SET ASIDE BY NAME:
      10.1016/j.fluid.2012.11.026: 2 pressure point(s), fewer than 5
      10.1016/j.jct.2015.07.024: 3 pressure point(s), fewer than 5
      10.1021/acs.jced.5b00064: 1 pressure point(s), fewer than 5
      10.1021/acs.jced.6b00085: 1 pressure point(s), fewer than 5
      10.1021/acs.jced.9b00068: 1 pressure point(s), fewer than 5
      10.1021/acs.jced.9b00430: 1 pressure point(s), fewer than 5
      10.1021/je049544x: 1 pressure point(s), fewer than 5

  FIT AND ACCEPTANCE (DEV.md 4c C283, Vitor 2026-11-10, declared before the fit).
  EVIDENCE: every study above is fitted; none is held out (C283 amended:
  laboratories disagree with each other by more than they claim, so the
  test is agreement across all of them, not one laboratory's claimed
  precision).  OBJECTIVE: `objective { method twoStage; }` -- least
  squares in log10 P for a first estimate, then the LARGEST relative error in
  P, (P_model - P)/P, over the kept points minimised from it (Vitor's
  practice, C280); both answers kept.  OUTLIERS: after the least-squares
  stage a point with a relative P error above 15 % (three times
  the acceptance) is DISCARDED BY NAME (its study DOI, T and P), listed in
  the result and the record, and the fit repeated without it, once
  (`outliers { maxRelativeError 15 percent; }`).  ACCEPTANCE,
  the DEFAULT of C283: ACCEPTED and promoted (autoPromoted, humanReviewed
  false) when the maximum relative P error over all kept points is at most
  5 % and the normal-boiling-point condition below holds with an
  absolute error below 1 K.  This case declares no
  `system/curationDict`, so the default applies; a case that needs another
  acceptance declares it there, with its reason.  The AmbroseWalton curve's
  errors on the same points are reported beside the fit's, as information.

  NORMAL BOILING POINT: the record's Tb 399.95 K is judged against the range of the KEPT points (all studies span 238.15-399.27 K before any outlier is discarded): if Tb lies OUTSIDE that range, the fitted Antoine's own normal boiling point (P = 101.325 kPa) must lie within the acceptance's temperature error of it, or the gap is announced and the fit is not promoted; inside it, the gap is reported and is not a condition.

  EARLIER FITS, SUPERSEDED BY THIS DECLARATION
  @@EARLIER-BEGIN@@
  C281 step 2, objective leastSquares (log10 P), the same partition and
  band: WHAT THE RUN FOUND (pinned in `expected`; measured, not argued).
  Antoine log10(Psat/bar) = 7.478412 - 3270.7603/(T + 53.2804), in-sample
  R2 0.999007 over 44 points, 273.1-315.2 K. HELD OUT: 42 points, AAD
  13.1956 % against the band 2 % -> notValidated. Its own normal boiling
  point (101.325 kPa): 384.41 K. NOT PROMOTED: held-out verdict
  notValidated (AAD 13.2 % against the band 2 % declared before the fit);
  the record keeps AmbroseWalton THEN C281 step 3, objective twoStage,
  one study fitted and one held out, judged by the band (superseded by
  C283): WHAT THE RUN FOUND (pinned in `expected`; measured, not argued).
  Objective twoStage. Antoine log10(Psat/bar) = 11.408700 - 6651.8995/(T
  + 204.3733), in-sample R2 0.998387 over 44 points, 273.1-315.2 K. HELD
  OUT: 42 points, AAD 25.8563 % (max 90.1072 %) against the band 2 % ->
  notValidated; the stage-1 least-squares answer on the same points: AAD
  13.1956 %, max 43.6593 %. Its own normal boiling point (101.325 kPa):
  378.97 K. NOT PROMOTED: held-out verdict notValidated (AAD 25.86 %
  against the band 2 % declared before the fit); the record keeps
  AmbroseWalton
  @@EARLIER-END@@

  NO MEASURED POINT IS IN THIS TREE: constant/archiveDatasets declares every
  series by DOI, NIST URL and sha256; `bin/choupo-curate fetch` regenerates
  them into constant/archiveExtracts/ (gitignored).

  RESULT
  @@RESULT-BEGIN@@
  WHAT THE RUN FOUND (pinned in `expected`; measured, not argued).
  Objective twoStage. Antoine log10(Psat/bar) = 4.174165 - 1387.2771/(T +
  -67.0909), in-sample R2 0.999868 over 167 kept points, 238.15-399.27 K
  (10.1016/j.jct.2008.02.012 44/44 kept; 10.1021/acs.jced.7b00295 42/42
  kept; 10.1021/je200784y 33/33 kept; 10.1021/je800984q 21/21 kept;
  10.1016/j.jct.2014.07.004 17/17 kept; 10.1021/acs.jced.7b00236 10/10
  kept). Relative error in P over the kept points: mean 2.2287 %, max
  7.5432 %; AmbroseWalton on the same points: mean 76.2139 %, max
  177.2845 %. Outliers discarded: none. Its own normal boiling point
  (101.325 kPa): 399.90 K. NOT PROMOTED by the DEFAULT acceptance of
  DEV.md 4c C283 (no system/curationDict): 6 studies, 167 points kept, 0
  discarded as outliers; max relative error 7.543 % (mean 2.229 %)
  against 5 %; AmbroseWalton on the same points mean 76.21 % / max 177.3
  %; the record keeps AmbroseWalton
  @@RESULT-END@@
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

operations
